    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Kyle Tucker** (77.96) and **Gunnar Henderson** (73.50), who represent our strongest offensive pillars. **Kyle Tucker** faces a generous matchup against McCullers Jr. (4.75 xERA), benefiting from a significant boost in SP skill projection that elevates his output. Meanwhile, **Gunnar Henderson** capitalizes on the combination of a favorable platoon advantage and a slow opposing delivery from P\u00e9rez, which creates an ideal environment for his elite speed tool to manifest in the stolen base column. **Jackson Merrill** (70.52) and **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) follow closely behind; **Sam Antonacci** in particular is a high-conviction play against Ure\u00f1a (5.17 xERA), where his elite xwOBA (.407) aligns perfectly with the soft matchup to generate maximum efficiency.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Nolan Schanuel** (55.01), who hovered on the fringe of the starting rotation but was ultimately squeezed out by the superior power-speed profiles of our primary starters. While **Nolan Schanuel** boasts an impressive SP skill efficiency (+17%), he lacks the aggressive lineup placement afforded to players like **Liam Hicks** or **Drake Baldwin**. Tactical adjustments continue to be necessary, particularly regarding **Heliot Ramos** (44.75), whose score is suppressed by a tough matchup against Rodriguez; however, he remains in the lineup due to the lack of a higher-projected replacement among our bench depth. We are monitoring **Josh Jung** (48.57) closely, as the 45% rain risk serves as a primary deterrent alongside his relatively stagnant matchup against Warren, making him a clear fade in favor of our more stable, high-efficiency options.",
